WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.606
The Purdue Model is a practical reference for understanding industrial architecture.

00:00:04.606 --> 00:00:09.521
It organizes functions from the physical process and basic control through supervisory

00:00:09.521 --> 00:00:11.979
and site operations to enterprise systems.

00:00:11.979 --> 00:00:17.713
The industrial DMZ adds a controlled buffer for necessary exchange between OT and IT.

00:00:17.713 --> 00:00:20.581
Each level has different responsibilities and consequences.

00:00:20.581 --> 00:00:25.906
Lower levels interact directly with equipment and require careful attention to safety, timing,

00:00:25.906 --> 00:00:26.725
and reliability.

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:30.412
Supervisory and site systems provide operator visibility, engineering authority,

00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:31.231
and coordination.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:35.327
Enterprise systems create business dependencies and potential pathways toward operations.

00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:40.242
Use the model to improve asset inventory, segmentation, access control, monitoring placement,

00:00:40.242 --> 00:00:42.290
remote-access design, and incident planning.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:46.796
Review data moving upward and commands, configurations, and administration moving downward.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:50.073
Make cross-level communication necessary, limited, observable, and owned.

00:00:50.073 --> 00:00:54.988
The model is not a perfect map or a substitute for engineering.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:59.085
Cloud platforms, industrial Internet of Things devices, vendors, remote sites,

00:00:59.085 --> 00:01:01.952
and converged architectures may cross traditional levels.

00:01:01.952 --> 00:01:03.590
Current diagrams, operational knowledge,

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.048
and environment-specific risk analysis remain essential.

00:01:06.048 --> 00:01:09.325
The strongest use of Purdue is shared reasoning.

00:01:09.325 --> 00:01:11.373
It helps security, engineering, operations,

00:01:11.373 --> 00:01:16.288
and business teams discuss how systems depend on one another and where

00:01:16.288 --> 00:01:18.337
controls should protect physical operations.

00:01:18.337 --> 00:01:21.613
Let the model guide questions and architecture decisions,

00:01:21.613 --> 00:01:25.300
while letting evidence and operational judgment determine the answer.
